A||||3||2birds||Valve lash adjustment on 2.8, timing questions also...||||1||
Z||000000||2birds||08-16-2001||12:20 AM||||So now that my heads are back on, I'm adjusting the valve lash.  The Haynes manual says to set #1 at Top Dead Center and twirl the pushrod until it drags (as you tighten the rocker arm nut), then go 1.5 additional turns on the rocker arm nut.  How much drag before you call it enough and give it the extra 1.5 turns?  <P>Which of the three slots in the balancer goes with cylinder #1?  I can't see any timing marks, other than three slots evenly spaced around the edge of the balancer.<BR>On the distributor cap, which terminal is #1 (I know, I'm a jackass, I should have labeled the wires...)||||reg||1
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||08-16-2001||02:20 AM||||Hopfully you still have the intake off as it is easier.<BR>Follow the steps in the book as you watch the center of the valve start to move down. From this point one more turn.<P>#1 TDC is marked on the balancer with the widest mark cut.||||reg||1
Z||000002||2birds||08-16-2001||10:57 AM||||I couldn't remember if TDC is when the ignition is supposed to occur, at the top of the compression stroke, or at the top of the exhaust stroke.  I checked the lash after the intake valve was fully closed but before the exhaust starts to open.  Last time I just backed the nut off four turns to get the pushrod in, and took it right back to the same spot, but since the heads came off and the valves were seated, I figure I ought to be a bit moe careful.<P>I'll check again for a wider slot in the balancer.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Indiana_resto_guy||08-16-2001||11:00 AM||||TDC is the top of the compression stroke.<BR>Both the intake and exhaust valves are fully closed. Pay particular attention to the valves you adjust in the sequence, don't get confused.<P>Luck||||reg||1
